help_intro = Fill the 9×9 grid so every row, every column, and every 3×3 box contains the digits 1 through 9 exactly once.
help_play = How to play
help_play_1 = • **Tap a cell** to select it.
help_play_2 = • **Tap a digit** in the keypad to fill the selected cell.
help_play_3 = • When the selected cell already contains a digit, that digit's key sinks in. Tap it again to clear the cell.
help_play_4 = • Use **notes mode** (the pencil) to mark candidate digits in a cell while you work out which numbers are still possible.
help_play_5 = • On a keyboard, type a digit to fill the selected cell, or **0** to clear it. The arrow keys move the selection.
help_checkpoint = Checkpoint
help_checkpoint_1 = • Tap **Checkpoint** to start a tentative session. Every digit you place after that point is shown in a distinctive color so you can tell experiment from confirmed work.
help_checkpoint_2 = • The Checkpoint button then splits into **Commit** (keep the placements and clear the highlight) and **Revert** (remove every checkpoint placement and return to where the session started).
help_undo = Undo and redo
help_undo_1 = • Tap **Undo** to take back the most recent move. After undoing, the button splits in two so you can **Redo**.
help_undo_2 = • Undo and redo are unlimited within the current puzzle. A new placement after an undo clears the redo history.
help_win = Hints and winning
help_win_1 = • The starting clues cannot be changed.
help_win_2 = • The timer runs while you play. Your **best time** for each difficulty is saved.
help_win_3 = • Some difficulties allow **hints**. Use them sparingly.
help_win_4 = • The puzzle is complete when every cell holds a valid digit and every row, column, and 3×3 box satisfies the no-repeat rule.
